why: the arc guards okay.http.Http, and the ONE real outbound path in
  this repo does not go through it: okay.llm.Transport is its own seam
  (post streaming lines back), so every LLM call in okay-demo, okay-agent
  and okay-chat gets no breaker, no limiter, no deadline. An LLM API is
  exactly what those exist for — 429 and 529 are routine there. And
  specs/resilience.md gates adaptive concurrency on "nothing wires
  Resilient.http into a service yet", which stays true until this lands.

what: Resilient.transport(inner, ...) in okay-resilience over the same
  five pieces (they are already generic over A ! Async; only the
  composed convenience was Http-shaped). Then okay-demo wires a breaker
  and a limiter around its Anthropic transport, which makes the arc a
  worked instance rather than a shelf. NOT converting the demo's five
  printlns: they are a startup banner and a login code for a human at a
  terminal, not service logging — checked, and Log would be wrong there.

